###  https://l-jamora.github.io/sdco#Cause
:Cause rdf:type owl:Class ;
       rdfs:subClassOf :Observation ;
       rdfs:comment """`Cause` is used to describe the characterization codes that define the cause of a defect.

Example: Surface Damage `BAF` char2 describes mechanical, chemical, [...] causes for the surface damage.

---


Created to describe BAF / DAF Surface Damage Char2.

Describes the cause of the surface damage. Has potential to be expanded to further describes other damage codes as well.

Also used to described BDG Loss of vision and its reasons for the vision obstruction to the view of the pipeline.

Also to describe DDC InspectionTermination Reasons"""@en ;
       rdfs:label "Cause"@en .


###  https://l-jamora.github.io/sdco#Channel
:Channel rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf :Inventory ;
         rdfs:comment """Used to describe DCI char1 and 2:

!Characterisation 1\"  The following information:  channel defective (A); channel not defective (B);  !no channel (C).\"

!Characterisation 2 Further information:  Channel narrows (in the direction of flow) (A); Channel widens (in the direction of flow) (B); Channel has a high point (C); Channel has a low point (D).\""""@en ;
         rdfs:label "Channel"@en .


